    "id": "2",
    "title": "10 Hidden Gems in Southeast Asia You Haven't Heard Of",
    "slug": "hidden-gems-southeast-asia",
    "excerpt": "Skip the tourist traps. These under-the-radar destinations in Southeast Asia will blow your mind — and your travel profile will thank you.",
    "coverImage": "https://cdn.travingat.com/landingpage-assets/blogs/blog-1775071028986.jpg",
    "content": "<p>Southeast Asia is one of the most popular travel regions in the world. But beyond the well-trodden paths of Bali, Bangkok, and Ha Long Bay, there are incredible places that most travelers never discover.</p><h2>1. Koh Rong Samloem, Cambodia</h2><p>Forget Koh Rong's party scene. Its quieter sister island, Koh Rong Samloem, offers pristine beaches with bioluminescent plankton that light up the water at night. It's pure magic.</p><h2>2. Hsipaw, Myanmar</h2><p>This small town in Shan State is the gateway to some of the most authentic trekking experiences in Asia. Walk through tea plantations, stay with local families, and witness a side of Myanmar that few tourists see.</p><figure><img src=\"https://cdn.travingat.com/landingpage-assets/images/testimonial-photo-figma.png\" alt=\"Hidden beach in Southeast Asia\"></figure><h2>3. Phong Nha, Vietnam</h2><p>Home to the world's largest cave (Son Doong), Phong Nha is an adventure lover's paradise. Even the more accessible caves here are absolutely spectacular.</p><p>The best part? All of these destinations look incredible on your Travingat profile. Organize them into a \"Hidden Gems\" collection and watch your friends ask for recommendations.</p>",
    "author": "Travingat Team",
    "publishedAt": "2026-02-28T10:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "southeast asia",
      "hidden gems",
      "adventure"
    ],
    "readTime": 6
  },
