    "id": "4",
    "title": "Beyond the Neon: A 2026 Guide to the Magic of Japan",
    "slug": "beyond-the-neon-a-2026-guide-to-the-magic-of-japan",
    "excerpt": "A journey through a country that holds both worlds in perfect tension\n",
    "coverImage": "https://cdn.travingat.com/landingpage-assets/blogs/blog-1775070718913.jpg",
    "content": "<div></div><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><div _ngcontent-ng-c3255093193=\"\" inline-copy-host=\"\" class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel enable-updated-hr-color\" id=\"model-response-message-contentr_bc71dc8f5c2efa6f\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-busy=\"false\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"caret-color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-style: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; white-space: normal; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-line: none; text-decoration-thickness: auto; text-decoration-style: solid; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><h1 data-path-to-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><br></h1><p data-path-to-node=\"1\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">If you’re reading this in<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"1\" data-index-in-node=\"26\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">April 2026</b>, you’re likely either in the middle of a cherry blossom whirlwind or planning a flight to the Land of the Rising Sun. Japan has always been a masterclass in contradiction—where 1,000-year-old temples sit in the shadow of skyscrapers—but 2026 is bringing some fresh energy to the archipelago.</p><p data-path-to-node=\"2\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Whether you're a first-timer or a seasoned traveler looking to escape the \"Golden Route\" crowds, here is how to navigate Japan right now.</p><hr data-path-to-node=\"3\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><h2 data-path-to-node=\"4\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">🌸 The Spring Sentinel: Sakura &amp; Beyond</h2><p data-path-to-node=\"5\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">We are currently in peak<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"5\" data-index-in-node=\"25\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Sakura (Cherry Blossom)</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>season! While Tokyo and Kyoto are the classic choices, 2026 is all about the \"Northern Sweep.\"</p><ul data-path-to-node=\"6\" style=\"padding-inline-start: 32px; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"6,0,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"6,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Pro Tip:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>If you missed the blooms in Tokyo (which peaked in late March), head north to<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"6,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"87\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Aomori</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>or<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"6,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"97\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Hokkaido</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>later this month.<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"6,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"124\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Hirosaki Park</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>is legendary for its \"flower rafts,\" where fallen petals turn the castle moat into a river of solid pink.</p></li><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"6,1,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"6,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">The 2026 Pivot:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Everyone goes for cherry blossoms, but late April brings the<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"6,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"77\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Fuji Shibazakura Festival</b>, where the ground at the base of Mt. Fuji is blanketed in 500,000 vibrant pink moss phlox. It’s a literal carpet of color.</p></li></ul><h2 data-path-to-node=\"7\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">🚄 Kansai’s New Era: Post-Expo Vibes</h2><p data-path-to-node=\"8\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Following the 2025 World Expo, the<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"8\" data-index-in-node=\"35\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Kansai region</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>(Osaka, Kyoto, Nara) has never been easier to navigate.</p><ul data-path-to-node=\"9\" style=\"padding-inline-start: 32px; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"9,0,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Osaka:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>The city has transformed. Check out the new developments on<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"9,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"67\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Yumeshima Island</b>, which are transitioning from Expo sites into a massive entertainment and luxury hub.</p></li><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"9,1,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Kyoto:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>To avoid the crowds, the move this year is<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"9,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"50\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">\"Early Morning Kyoto.\"</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Arrive at the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove or Fushimi Inari at 6:30 AM. You’ll have the silence to yourself before the tour buses arrive at 9:00 AM.</p></li></ul><h2 data-path-to-node=\"10\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">🍙 The 2026 \"Slow Travel\" Hit List</h2><p data-path-to-node=\"11\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Overtourism is a real conversation this year, so travelers are looking for \"Deep Japan.\" If you want the soul of the country without the elbow-to-elbow crowds, check out these spots:</p><ul data-path-to-node=\"12\" style=\"padding-inline-start: 32px; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"12,0,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"12,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Tohoku:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Explore rugged landscapes, ancient hot spring towns, and a more \"traditional\" feel that's hard to find in the big cities.</p></li><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"12,1,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"12,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Kyushu:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Home to<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"12,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"16\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Mt. Aso</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>(a massive active caldera) and incredible street-side ramen stalls in Fukuoka.</p></li><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"12,2,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"12,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Shikoku:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Perfect for cyclists and those looking to find Zen while walking portions of the famous 88-temple pilgrimage.</p></li><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"12,3,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"12,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">PokéPark Kanto:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Opening this year! The world’s first permanent Pokémon theme park is a must for the young (and young at heart).</p></li></ul><hr data-path-to-node=\"13\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><h2 data-path-to-node=\"14\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">🥢 Eating Your Way Through the Islands</h2><p data-path-to-node=\"15\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">You can’t write a Japan blog without mentioning the food. This year, the trend is<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"15\" data-index-in-node=\"82\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Regional Gastronomy</b>.</p><ul data-path-to-node=\"16\" style=\"padding-inline-start: 32px; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"16,0,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"16,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Don't just eat Ramen:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Seek out<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"16,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"31\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Okonomiyaki</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>in Hiroshima (layered, not mixed!), or head to<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"16,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"90\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Hokkaido</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>for the freshest uni (sea urchin) and king crab you’ll ever taste.</p></li><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"16,1,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"16,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">The \"Convenience\" Hack:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Never underestimate a<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><i data-path-to-node=\"16,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"46\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Konbini</i><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>(convenience store) run. The 2026 seasonal limited-edition snacks are currently all about strawberry and sakura flavors!</p></li></ul><h2 data-path-to-node=\"17\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">💡 Travel Quick-Tips for 2026</h2><ol start=\"1\" data-path-to-node=\"18\" style=\"padding-inline-start: 32px; font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"18,0,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"18,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Digital Entry:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Ensure your<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><b data-path-to-node=\"18,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"27\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Visit Japan Web</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>QR codes are ready before you land to breeze through customs.</p></li><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"18,1,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"18,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">The JR Pass:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Remember that prices increased significantly recently. Unless you are crisscrossing the entire country in a week, individual tickets or regional passes often offer better value now.</p></li><li style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"18,2,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"18,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Cash is (Still) King-ish:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>While major cities are more card-friendly than ever, those charming mountain<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><i data-path-to-node=\"18,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"103\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">ryokans</i><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>and local ramen shops still love their yen.</p></li></ol><hr data-path-to-node=\"19\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><blockquote data-path-to-node=\"20\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><p data-path-to-node=\"20,0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"20,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Final Thought:</b><span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span>Japan isn't just a place you see; it’s a place you<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">&nbsp;</span><i data-path-to-node=\"20,0\" data-index-in-node=\"66\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">feel</i>. It’s the bow of a station master, the steam rising off an outdoor onsen in the snow, and the hushed silence of a mossy shrine.</p></blockquote><p data-path-to-node=\"21\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\"><b data-path-to-node=\"21\" data-index-in-node=\"0\" style=\"font-family: &quot;Google Sans Text&quot;, sans-serif !important; line-height: 1.15 !important; margin-top: 0px !important;\">Are you planning a trip for the upcoming summer festivals, or are you aiming for the fiery red maples of autumn?</b></p></div><div><p class=\"p24\" style=\"text-align: center; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-language-override: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 15px; line-height: normal; font-family: &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;; color: rgb(187, 152, 88); -webkit-text-stroke-color: rgb(187, 152, 88); letter-spacing: normal;\"><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-kerning: none;\"></span></p></div>",
